	(text "Current-sink channel (4 instances, one TLV9154 section each)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.0 22.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 4.5 4.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 40 90 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d8ee19b9-4162-5217-96ed-1c4db9b6d8f6")
	)
	(text "Each MOSFET gets its own loop forced to V_SET / 0.1 R, so current and power share equally whatever the threshold spread."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.0 26.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(italic yes)
				(color 70 70 70 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fc5d525a-dd3f-5b88-9483-5c06828dcfe8")
	)
	(text "Rs: two 0.2 R 2512 in parallel = 0.1 R, so I_ch = V_SET / 0.1 R (2.56 A full scale).\nKELVIN: Rn03 and Rn08 connect at the TOP PAD of the Rs pair on their own trace, never\nalong the high-current source copper. Rg within 10 mm of the gate pin. Dn03 and Rn05 sit\nat the FET pins. Dn02 limits integrator wind-up; Rn02 (15M) gives +2.6 mV offset, above the\nTLV9154 0.83 mV Vos limit, so DAC code 0 is truly 0 A (dead zone about 106 mA in total, 42\ncodes). Loop values from rev_e deck 03: PM >= 87 deg, GM >= 22 dB for the IRFP250N / 240 / 530\n(the big-die IXTH proxy drops to 80 deg / 9 dB). Change them only with a re-run of deck 03.\n(n = channel number)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 90.04 185.05 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "56ef4a50-a003-5d39-8fc5-8cc393f7fdbe")
	)
	(text "Channel (one of four): TLV9154 section, 3.3k / 1n / 47R compensation, IRFP250N, 2 x 0.2R Kelvin sense"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 85.82 46.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5e2b9280-0553-5cf1-ad3b-1e1ba8805f97")
	)
	(text "Same nets, second names (KILL_T = KILL ...). Channel 4 leaves KILL_T, VSET_T and AVG_T open; its DRAIN_T\ncarries DRAIN on to the dropout comparator. Electrically every channel still hangs directly on the four nets."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 150.04 217.05 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ca94a789-8a68-5cdd-8a94-9f030a1ba6e5")
	)
	(text "Chain pins: the four channels are daisy-chained on page 1 (each net enters on the left and leaves on the right)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 93.44 205.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4e2899ce-1f36-575f-a984-5095852e04b8")
	)
